         new="Then C1 and C3 are contradictory at $t^{*} = t_\\pi(a) + 6$ by the argument above, provided C3 reaches the record. *Where it does, no erasure request is required.* It does so when the log entry is itself electronic health data within the environment, which, on the reading set out below, is the case for logs kept at patient-record granularity and not for logs kept at dataset granularity. For such records the infeasibility follows from two provisions of a single regulation acting on a single environment. Article 73(1)(e) requires the identifiable log to remain verifiable for twelve months, and Article 68(12) requires the electronic health data within the environment to be deleted six months after permit expiry.",
